Source package: gtk+3.0

wayland-export-xdg-toplevel.patch
    Backport of GTK commit edc9d508c3 (merge request 9852), which is on the gtk-3-24 branch but in no
    release yet, while Ubuntu 26.04 ships 3.24.52. A GdkWaylandWindow emits xdg-toplevel-realized when
    its xdg_toplevel is created, before it is committed, and gdk_wayland_window_get_xdg_toplevel()
    returns it. Firefox needs both for Wayland session restore, to name a window to the compositor
    before the window is first shown, and turns session restore off when the signal is missing
    (IsSessionRestoreSupported in its widget/gtk/nsAppShell.cpp). It works together with the patches
    in patches/firefox/ and patches/mutter/.

    The commit adds no test, and none is added here. GTK's test suite runs during the build, which
    shows the patch breaks nothing existing; that the signal works is shown by Firefox registering its
    windows, see patches/firefox/README.

wayland-export-xdg-toplevel-symbols.patch (debian-series)
    Lists the new function in debian/libgtk-3-0t64.symbols. dh_makeshlibs runs with -c4, which fails
    the build on any exported symbol the file does not list. It changes the packaging, so it is
    applied from debian-series rather than series.

run-clipboard-tests-alone.patch
    Makes the build's test suite run the clipboard and textbuffer tests with no other test at the same
    time. All tests share the one X display xvfb-run starts for them, and both tests copy and paste
    through its CLIPBOARD selection. When one takes the selection while the other is between a copy and
    a paste, the paste goes through the X server and has not arrived when textbuffer checks the text,
    so textbuffer fails now and then, which fails the build. Next to clipboard running in a loop,
    textbuffer failed 5 of 300 runs, and alone none. The patch is local only and changes only how the
    tests are scheduled.

Drop wayland-export-xdg-toplevel.patch and wayland-export-xdg-toplevel-symbols.patch once Ubuntu
ships a GTK 3 with the commit, which is any 3.24.53 or newer, after checking that its symbols file
lists gdk_wayland_window_get_xdg_toplevel. Keep run-clipboard-tests-alone.patch while the test suite
runs clipboard and textbuffer next to other tests.

Check by hand after an upgrade:

  nm -D /usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libgdk-3.so.0 | grep xdg_toplevel     should list gdk_wayland_window_get_xdg_toplevel
